  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 131 PM EDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\nChilly morning today with temperatures dropping back into the 30's \nfor many cities. Still will need a light jacket for the next several \nmornings, but a warming trend is starting which will help bring \nmorning lows into the 40's for most and afternoon highs in the 70's. \nDew points in the 40's and 50's mean we'll have dry weather which \nwill be a nice break from the humidity of the past several months. \nI'm not a arborist, but I imagine we'll also see much leaf change \ncolor this week.\n\nClear skies, light winds, and extremely pleasant temperatures are \nexpected for the next 7 days. High pressure sets up and looks to \nremain in place. These are the fall days most people out here hope \nfor, couldn't ask for nicer weather.",
